==Strategy==
Luckily, Brollow variants are only the ''[[March to Death (Merciless)|second]]'' most annoying thing that can be combined with Daboo, and they spawn in limited quantities so this stage remains manageable. Stalling the startoff is tricky, since Owlbrow is the only enemy that can't [[Revive]] or [[Burrow]], making it very easy to push past everything and hit the enemy base.

Once Daboo does spawn, his support is not enough to keep him from being swarmed. Basic [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie Cats]], or general meatshields like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] can keep him near the base, while fast attackers like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], and [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]] help Shigong deal damage to the boss and clear the support. Two Zollows will spawn, but they will die quickly to most attackers; the [[Holy Blast]] can help if they are still an issue, along with helping to Z-kill Daboo.

Teacher Bun Bun can add some difficulty, but even if he does push, there is plenty of room to chip him down as he advances. When dealing with him, [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] units like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] are helpful. More realistically, he will just be bursted down along with Daboo.

